; Supply-chain protection: only install package versions that have been
; published for at least 21 days (3 weeks). Freshly-published malicious
; releases are refused, so they have time to be detected/pulled before we
; ever install them. npm installs the newest version that satisfies the
; age requirement; asking for a too-new exact version errors out.
;
; NOTE: requires npm >= 11.10.0 (which needs Node >= 20.17). Older npm
; (e.g. the 9.x currently in use) silently ignores this key, so upgrade
; npm/Node for it to take effect. Do not combine with `--before`.
min-release-age=21
